  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{3}^{t-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{{3}^{t-1}\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613},5\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{3}^{t-1},5\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\u27e8{3}^{2-1},5\u27e9=\u27e83,5\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=2$ is $\\sqrt{34}.$",
